## Company facts (from Victor, 2026-08-25)

- Mozentai is an engineering company. Public copy is generic toward software engineers. Lead public pitch (2026-09-19): "Stop wasting time on screening." We prepare the professionals for the companies so they do not waste time on screening. Look them up on the Career Wall. Engagement models: staff aug, dedicated team, project-based. Tagline: Engineers @ Work.
- **CITC** (Council of Information Technology & Computing): professional standing for software engineers, CREA/CRM analog. Public copy stays English. Do not print CREA/CRM, CPF, $20, $200, or "five titles" on the site. Mechanics below are real and must be followed in product work.

### CITC mechanics (Victor, 2026-09-19, not for the public page)

- **Identifier:** Each registered engineer (and each company) holds a SmartHex-16 number, the CITC CREA analog of CPF/CREA. Package: PyPI `smarthex` 0.2.2 by Victor Matos (contact@byteram.co), repo Byteram/SmartHex16. 16 hex chars: 14 random + 2 checksum. Generate/validate via `from smarthex import generate, validate`. Local checkout: `~/github/pypi-env/smarthex`. Example valid IDs generated 2026-09-19: `3f3ed5d05b617d16`, `529532bed881a1c9`, `331023a6abff6ed1`. Display on the wall as "CITC number", not "SmartHex".
- **Stripe is the source of standing.** CREA keep-alive and company plans are Stripe Billing. Title exams are Stripe one-time Checkout. Verify every webhook with the `Stripe-Signature` header. A CREA is live only while the keep-alive subscription is active. A title is granted only after the exam payment (and Mozentai's own pass/fail). Companies are likewise Stripe customers. Do not treat a SmartHex as valid without a matching signed Stripe event.
- **Engineer keep-alive:** USD 20 per month to keep the CREA. Stripe Checkout `mode: 'subscription'`. One Product named CITC CREA with one recurring Price $20/month. Do not put other tiers on that Product. Never pass `payment_method_types`. Latest Stripe API `2026-07-29.dahlia`. Restricted key (`rk_`) not `sk_`. Customer Portal for cancel/update. If charging US or EU, Stripe Tax needs an active registration before `automatic_tax`.
- **Title exam:** USD 200 to take the test for a given title. Stripe Checkout `mode: 'payment'`, one-time. One Product per exam code (P1, P2, P3, later PX and other titles) each with a $200 Price so Checkout line items show the exam name. Cap: **5 titles per CREA**. An engineer cannot hold everything under the sun.
- **Exam names (Victor, 2026-09-19):** Python titles use P1, P2, P3. Any code ending in **X** is specialist (PX for Python specialist). Do not invent a specialist title on the public catalog until Victor names it. Public wall shows P1, P2, P3 on the three Python Engineer cards.
- **Question groups:** Each level/title has its own question bank. Author them in `_data/exams.yml` under that exam code. Do not invent questions. Do not render the bank on mozentai.com.
- **Performance type:** After a sitting, generate a performance type from the candidate's test score. Do not invent score bands or type names until Victor supplies them. Same score-to-type step for both exam modes.
- **Two exam modes:** (1) Regular questionnaire. (2) Live with a tester: the candidate schedules the sitting and takes it with an instructor. Internal analogy is Hack The Box style practical work, but CITC is scheduled with an instructor, not a self-serve HTB box. Never print "Hack The Box", HTB, score bands, or the question bank on the public site. Public copy may say questionnaire or schedule a session with an instructor.
- **Public title catalog on 2026-09-19:** 1. Python Engineer I (exam P1)  2. Python Engineer II (exam P2)  3. Python Engineer III (exam P3). Requirements (exigencias) come only from Mozentai. Engineers look those titles up as what they want to become. They do not get a menu of outside credentials.
- **Career Wall:** Once registered, the engineer appears on the wall and can be looked up (name, CITC number, title, or exam). Do not invent people. Do not put Victor on the wall. Photos in `assets/engineers/`. Portraits must use site colors only (`--bg`, `--surface`, `--accent`, `--muted`, `--text`). No photographic color. CSS grayscale + mint color wash.
- **Company access:** Companies do not get the whole roster. Stripe plan determines which engineer group they can access. Public wall is lookup/display. Hiring access is plan-gated.
- **Engineer access:** Engineers see their own CREA and Mozentai titles/exigencias. They look up what they want to be. They do not browse every other engineer.
- **Public site:** Know the mechanics. Do not print prices, the five-title cap, Stripe, SmartHex, CPF, CREA, CRM, PX, Hack The Box, score bands, or exam questions on mozentai.com.
- Mozentai has been in the market for 10 years.
- Specialists have 15+ years of hands-on security experience. Do not publish a 10+ band on the site; Victor corrected this to 15+ only on 2026-08-25.
- **CEO:** Victor Matos (professional name; full name Victor Vinicius Reis de Matos). Photo: `assets/team/victor-matos.jpg`.
- **Hack The Box:** public profile [spacemany2k38](https://profile.hackthebox.com/profile/019cab82-c302-71b6-a445-abbfbbb76b89) (UUID `019cab82-c302-71b6-a445-abbfbbb76b89`). Handle `@spacemany2k38`. HTB is **not** linked from the public site as of 2026-09-19 (Leadership section removed). If it returns, show credential as abbreviated "HTB CJCA" only, NEVER expand to "Junior" on the site (Victor is an expert, not junior-level). Do not paste the HTB About text (Avenue Code, Axonius, etc.) onto mozentai.com. Link out. Strip `utm_*` from the URL. Never mention Bitly on this public site.
- Do not invent extra stats (audit counts, retention %, countries served) unless Victor supplies them. A previous INOTVMOS-inspired stats set (2,400+ fixes, 98% retention, 120+ audits, 14 countries) was marketing filler and was replaced.

